1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,000
[roars]

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,000
[narrator]
Strange beasts

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,000
and monsters.

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,000
[squeaking]

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Vast riches.

6
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Hidden treasures.

7
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Evil haunts.

8
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Uncharted frontiers.

9
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
The mysterious unknown.

10
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
The people who are captivated by
the magic in those words

11
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
are called…

12
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Hunters.

13
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,000
[theme music playing]

14
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:53,000
[music concludes]

15
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:56,000
[grunts]

16
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,000
[Kurapika]
We entered the long and difficult path,

17
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,000
broke down the wall,

18
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,000
and from there we snuck into
the short and easy one.

19
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Even under pressure, you were able
to calmly assess our options,

20
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,000
and think of a way
to get around them.

21
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:14,000
And that is what makes you so special.

22
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:19,000
HIT x THE x TARGET

23
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:25,000
[narrator] One by one,
each of the 24 applicants who passed

24
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:29,000
the Third Phase of
the Hunter Exam exited Trick Tower,

25
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:32,000
eager for a long awaited breath
of fresh air.

26
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:37,000
[tense music playing]

27
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,000
-Oh.
-[chuckles]

28
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:53,000
-Huh?
-[chuckles]

29
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,000
Congratulations on escaping
Trick Tower, everyone.

30
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:02,000
All that remain now are
the Fourth Phase and the Final Phase.

31
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,000
Only two more.

32
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:09,000
The Fourth Phase will take place
right over there on Zevil Island.

33
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,000
Now, let's proceed.

34
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:16,000
[applicants murmuring]

35
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:20,000
To begin with I will need each of you
to draw lots now.

36
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:22,000
-[surprised gasping]
-Really?

37
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:25,000
Draw lots for what?
What will that decide?

38
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:27,000
[chuckles softly]

39
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:29,000
Who you hunt, and who hunts you.

40
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:34,000
In this box are exactly
24 numbered cards.

41
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Which means,

42
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:39,000
that one of the numbered cards
will correspond with your badge.

43
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:45,000
Now, each of you will draw a card
in the order you exited the tower.

44
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,000
All right. Which of you was first?

45
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,000
[indistinct murmuring]

46
00:03:59,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Hmm.

47
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,000
[cards rattling]

48
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:12,000
[rattling noises]

49
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,000
Guess that means I'm next.

50
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:25,000
After him, I'm next.

51
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,000
-Oh, hey, Killua.
-Huh?

52
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:37,000
He mentioned us hunting and being hunted.

53
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:40,000
Do you think that means
we're gonna be fighting each other?

54
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:42,000
Yeah, probably does.

55
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,000
[whistles]

56
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:14,000
Now, I don't know
what this is all about,

57
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,000
but I know you've got to draw it
like you mean it.

58
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Yeah!

59
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,000
[Lippo]
Has everyone drawn?

60
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:36,000
Very well. Now if you would,
please go ahead and remove the sticker.

61
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:47,000
Hmm.

62
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:49,000
The number you see is your target.

63
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:51,000
[applicants gasping]

64
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:55,000
[breathes heavily]

65
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,000
[breathes shakingly]

66
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:06,000
This box has recorded the number
that each of you drew.

67
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:10,000
Each card was tallied
and then stored in memory.

68
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:11,000
So if you like,

69
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:16,000
you're free to dispose of the cards.
It makes no difference at this point.

70
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:20,000
The objective is to steal
your target's ID badge.

71
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,000
Oh, good.

72
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,000
So we don't have to kill each other, then.

73
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:28,000
The method is up to you.
Procure the badge however you see fit.

74
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:33,000
But if you kill your target,
you can take their badge easily.

75
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:37,000
Yeah, that sure sounds like
the fastest way to me.

76
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:39,000
[nervously] So that's how it's gonna be?

77
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:41,000
Come on, there's nothing to be scared of.

78
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:43,000
[Lippo]
Listen carefully!

79
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:47,000
Collecting the ID badge
of your specified target

80
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:49,000
will earn you three points. Understand?

81
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:53,000
Your own badge is also worth three points.

82
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:57,000
And all the other badges
are worth one point.

83
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:02,000
In order to move on to the Final Phase,
you will have to collect six points.

84
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:05,000
So during your time there on Zevil Island,

85
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:09,000
gather enough badges to collect six points
or fail the exam.

86
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:15,000
Only those who do will clear
the Fourth Phase of the Hunter Exam.

87
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:24,000
[woman] I'd like to commend all of you
on your work in the exam's third phase.

88
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:30,000
I'll be your guide. It's nice to meet you.
You can call me Khara.

89
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:35,000
It will take two hours for this boat
to reach its destination, Zevil Island.

90
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:40,000
All 24 applicants who've made it this far
are granted an open invitation

91
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:44,000
to participate again in next year's exam
no matter what.

92
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:48,000
So even if you don't pass this time,
we really hope you'll try again.

93
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:51,000
Never say die, right… everybody?

94
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:56,000
[faltering] Wow, that went over well.

95
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,000
It appears the battle has already begun.

96
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:03,000
You're right.

97
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:05,000
Everybody has already taken off
their badges

98
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:08,000
and tucked them away
so they won't get stolen yet.

99
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:10,000
All right, everyone.

100
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:13,000
For the next two hours,
you're all free to do whatever you like.

101
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:17,000
Thank you, and I hope you all enjoy
the rest of the voyage.

102
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:20,000
Hmm?

103
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:26,000
[grunts] So, uh,

104
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,000
hypothetically,

105
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:31,000
if you happened to be my target, I mean…

106
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:34,000
Don't expect me to show you any mercy,
okay?

107
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:35,000
Well, of course not.

108
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:38,000
If you happened to be my target…

109
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:40,000
-[shrieks]
-…I would say the same thing to you.

110
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:42,000
Am I your target? Really?

111
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:46,000
[chuckles] I'm speaking hypothetically.

112
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:49,000
Oh yeah, I knew that.
We're speaking hypothetically.

113
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:51,000
[chuckles softly] You needn't worry.

114
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:54,000
You're not my target, Leorio.

115
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,000
Oh, I see.

116
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:58,000
[hesitates] Oh! So you know,
you're not my target, either.

117
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,000
[Kurapika chuckles]

118
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:04,000
[seagulls squawking]

119
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:06,000
-Hey.
-Hmm?

120
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:19,000
So, uh… who did you get?

121
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:21,000
What did you draw?

122
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,000
It's a secret.

123
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:24,000
[Gon grunts]

124
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:29,000
[both laugh]

125
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:31,000
Don't worry about it.

126
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:33,000
You're not my target, Gon. I promise.

127
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,000
That's good.
Because you're not mine, either.

128
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:41,000
You want to show our numbers
at the same time?

129
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:43,000
Okay.

130
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,000
[Gon and Killua] Ready, and!

131
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:47,000
[gasps]

132
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,000
[Killua] Number 44 is…

133
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:54,000
[Gon] Really?

134
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:59,000
You've got seriously bad luck.

135
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:01,000
[chuckles] Oh, do you think so?

136
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:05,000
So, who is number 199, anyway?

137
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:08,000
-I'm not sure, I thought maybe you knew.
-Nope.

138
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:10,000
If I'd have just been smarter about it,

139
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:12,000
I would have memorized
everybody's numbers.

140
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:16,000
Once he explained it,
that's when I started paying attention.

141
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:19,000
But everyone had taken off
their badges already.

142
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:21,000
-[Gon grunts]
-Pretty lame, huh?

143
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:25,000
[breathes shakily]

144
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:28,000
-Gon.
-[gasps]

145
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:29,000
Oh, what's up?

146
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:34,000
Are you happy or scared right now?
Which one is it?

147
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:36,000
Hmm.

148
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:41,000
Kind of both, I guess.

149
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:48,000
If I had to fight with Hisoka one-on-one,
I wouldn't stand a chance against him.

150
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:52,000
But if all I have to do
is just steal his badge,

151
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:55,000
I don't know,
I think I might actually have a real shot.

152
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,000
Yeah.

153
00:10:57,000 --> 00:11:01,000
The way it is now,
well, at least I've got a chance.

154
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:04,000
And to be honest,
it does scare me a little bit.

155
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:07,000
But I think it's worth it.

156
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:10,000
I gotcha.

157
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,000
Well, let's do our best.

158
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:20,000
Don't die, okay?

159
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:22,000
Yeah, and same to you.

160
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:32,000
[Khara]
Thanks for being patient, everyone.

161
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:34,000
We've arrived at Zevil Island!

162
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:36,000
Okay then.

163
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:39,000
You will be disembarking in the order
you completed the Third Phase,

164
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:41,000
from the shortest to the longest.

165
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:43,000
[grunts] Not this again.

166
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:46,000
You'll go ashore one at a time,

167
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:49,000
with two minute intervals separating
each of the applicants, all right?

168
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,000
I guess that means
we'll be waiting here a while.

169
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:54,000
Yeah.

170
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:56,000
[Khara] You'll be on the island
exactly one week.

171
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:59,000
That means you only have seven days

172
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:02,000
to collect your six points
and then return to this location.

173
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:06,000
First applicant,
get ready to disembark now.

174
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:10,000
[thrilling music playing]

175
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:17,000
Now I understand.

176
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,000
The first to go ashore have the advantage.

177
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:23,000
Right. They can hide
and watch everyone's movements,

178
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:25,000
including their target's,
before they make their move.

179
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:30,000
That's two minutes.
The second person may go.

180
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:31,000
-[rattling noises]
-[Khara whimpers]

181
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:33,000
[gasps]

182
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:38,000
The third person may go.

183
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:40,000
Yeah, all right!

184
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:42,000
[Khara] The seventh person.

185
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:44,000
The eleventh person.

186
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:47,000
The fifteenth person!

187
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:50,000
The twentieth person may go.

188
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,000
[music continues]

189
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:58,000
That's two minutes.
The twenty-first person may go.

190
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:01,000
-Bye.
-Bye.

191
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:08,000
Okay.

192
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:11,000
I guess I'll start off
by scouting the island.

193
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:16,000
That's two minutes.
The twenty-second person may go.

194
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:18,000
Great!

195
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,000
-See ya.
-Good luck.

196
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,000
[Gon]
First, I've got to find Hisoka.

197
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:32,000
HUNTER GLOSSARY

198
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:36,000
ZEVIL ISLAND

199
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:39,000
[pensive music playing]

200
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:47,000
[Gon]
How am I going to steal Hisoka's badge?

201
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:52,000
Such a good boy.

202
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:55,000
[grunts]

203
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:57,000
Very nice.

204
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:01,000
I'm beginning to get excited.

205
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:03,000
[gasps]

206
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:04,000
[choking]

207
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:09,000
[gasps, coughs]

208
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:12,000
Hmm.

209
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:19,000
I definitely can't get his badge
in a head-to-head fight.

210
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:20,000
Oh.

211
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:23,000
[music stops]

212
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:27,000
[gasping]

213
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:29,000
It's an applicant.

214
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,000
And there's another one behind him.

215
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:38,000
[grunts]

216
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:40,000
[Gon]
He's targeting the guy in front.

217
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:49,000
[grunts]

218
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:56,000
Oh.

219
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:05,000
[breathes heavily]

220
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:08,000
[both grunting]

221
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:12,000
[yelps, groans]

222
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:14,000
[Gon]
He missed!

223
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:19,000
That was close. A little too close, even.

224
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:25,000
Sorry, pal, but I don't go down…
[falters] …that easy.

225
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:29,000
[groaning] What the…

226
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:34,000
[trembling] You bastard.

227
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:38,000
I coated the arrow with
a fast-acting tranquilizer.

228
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:41,000
So you're not going to be able
to walk much for about a week.

229
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:43,000
Don't worry, though.

230
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:47,000
There's fresh water nearby.
So you probably won't die.

231
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:50,000
But I'll be taking this, of course.

232
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:52,000
Later!

233
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:56,000
[Gon] Wow.

234
00:15:57,000 --> 00:16:01,000
He was able to hide his presence
while he quietly stalked his prey.

235
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:07,000
And his target sensed the shot being fired
and was able to dodge it,

236
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:10,000
avoiding what would've been
a serious injury.

237
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,000
But the stalker had that covered,

238
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:15,000
coating his arrow with poison.

239
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:19,000
So that's how you hunt!

240
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:30,000
If I'm going to have any chance
of stealing Hisoka's badge,

241
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:32,000
that's the only way.

242
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:36,000
[repeating swishing]

243
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:43,000
First, I'll have to sneak up on him
without being noticed,

244
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:47,000
and wait for my chance,

245
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:48,000
and take it!

246
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:52,000
All right!

247
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:57,000
[grunts]

248
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:01,000
But this target's not moving
like Hisoka will be.

249
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:04,000
[sighs]

250
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:08,000
Either way, I'll only get one shot.

251
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:12,000
I've got to hook his badge
while he's not paying attention,

252
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:13,000
or I don't stand a chance.

253
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:19,000
[grunts] Okay.

254
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:26,000
Try to read his movements.

255
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:32,000
And now!

256
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:42,000
[grunts]

257
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:48,000
Aw. This won't do it.

258
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:52,000
It's way too easy
to follow a swinging target.

259
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:55,000
I already know exactly
where it's gonna go.

260
00:17:58,000 --> 00:17:59,000
[croaks]

261
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:04,000
Oh!

262
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:06,000
That's right.

263
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:10,000
I've got to remember,
he'll try to move out of the way.

264
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,000
[water burbling]

265
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:25,000
If I can't catch a flying bird
by watching how it moves,

266
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,000
then I'll never be able to steal
Hisoka's badge.

267
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,000
[grunts]

268
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:40,000
Almost.

269
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:42,000
Oh well.

270
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:45,000
I really can't expect to catch a bird
on my very first try.

271
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,000
[yelling] There! All right!

272
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:49,000
[grunting]

273
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:56,000
[sighs]

274
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:01,000
Got to figure out whose number this is.

275
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:08,000
The sun is just about to set.

276
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:12,000
I should probably stay in one location
until morning.

277
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:16,000
[panting]

278
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:24,000
Damn. I didn't think
all this was going to be so hard.

279
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:25,000
[grunts]

280
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:28,000
It's way too dark for me to see anything.

281
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:31,000
And there aren't any birds out anymore.

282
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:33,000
Guess I'll start fresh in the morning!

283
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:41,000
[birds chirping]

284
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:46,000
[sputtered grunting]

285
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:50,000
All right, now it's back to training!

286
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:53,000
[grunts]

287
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:03,000
[panting]

288
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:04,000
It's hopeless.

289
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:07,000
Maybe this is impossible.

290
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:12,000
Catching a bird mid-flight… accurately?

291
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:14,000
What was I even thinking?

292
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:16,000
-[water splashing]
-Hm?

293
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:18,000
[gasps]

294
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:26,000
But if a bird can catch a fish
while it's swimming…

295
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:31,000
[grunts]

296
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:41,000
There it goes!

297
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:50,000
That's it!

298
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:52,000
That's the key.

299
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:56,000
That's how I can tell
when my target's going to move.

300
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:05,000
[grunts]

301
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:17,000
Now! [grunts]

302
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:19,000
[triumphant music playing]

303
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:21,000
I did it!

304
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:23,000
I figured it out!

305
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:27,000
I've just got to go for the target
the moment it goes for its prey.

306
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:33,000
[man] Huh, the kid's impressive.

307
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:36,000
He actually mastered the art of the hunt.

308
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:42,000
But concentration like that
will come back to bite you. [snickers]

309
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:49,000
[narrator] Gon finally mastered the trick
that would aid him in his hunt for Hisoka.

310
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:52,000
However, unbeknownst to him,

311
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:54,000
Gon was being hunted himself.

312
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:57,000
[music concludes]

313
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:00,000
[theme music playing]

314
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:17,000
[music concludes]

315
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:19,000
[thrilling music playing]

316
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:23,000
DO NOT FEED!

317
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:25,000
[Gon] Next time.
"Explosion of Deception."

318
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:27,000
-Explode!
-[Killua] Explode!

319
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:28,000
[Gon] Kaboom!

320
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:29,000
[Killua] Oh, mushroom.

321
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:32,000
Subtitle translation by
Mitsuko Kitajima
